    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Bryce Harper** (70.17) stands as our premier play, capitalizing on a favorable matchup against a lefty and wind conditions at his back to maximize his ceiling. Alongside him, **Luis Arraez** (66.78), **Taylor Ward** (66.63), and **Jung Hoo Lee** (63.63) anchor our offensive core. **Arraez**, **Lee**, and **Drew Gilbert** all benefit from an optimal matchup against Luinder Avila, whose high-xERA profile offers significant volume potential. **Gleyber Torres** (64.55) maintains a strong efficiency score despite the rain risk, as his platoon advantage against David Peterson offsets the localized weather concerns. Meanwhile, **Jonathan Aranda** (61.34) earns his spot in the UTIL slot by successfully navigating Kevin Gausman\u2019s 3.76 xERA through a highly favorable platoon split.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Dylan Beavers** (50.69). While he presented a decent floor, he narrowly missed the cut due to a negative L/L platoon disadvantage and the optimizer's preference for **Gavin Sheets** (60.09) in the outfield, who carries a cleaner matchup profile against Reynaldo L\u00f3pez. We are monitoring **Gleyber Torres** closely; his 41% rain risk is the primary yellow flag on the board today. Furthermore, while **Masyn Winn** (58.97) remains in the lineup for his defensive floor and potential on the basepaths, we are cautious about his matchup against a pitcher with a 4.62 xERA despite the presence of a catcher with a 1.89s pop time, which limits his stolen base upside. We remain heavily indexed toward high-speed profiles to address our scarcity in the SB category, keeping players like **Jung Hoo Lee** and **Luis Arraez** in high-leverage roles despite the occasional SP threat.",
